Start()
start() is a method of the Thread class that creates a new thread and starts its execution.
When you call start(), Java creates a new thread and automatically calls the run() method.
Thread methods

Syntax
thread.start();
example
MyThread t = new MyThread();(object creation)
t.start();(create a new thread)
Run()
run() is the method that contains the code or task to be executed by the thread.
When a thread starts, the run() method is executed automatically.
Syntax
public void run() {
    // Code to execute
}

sleep(milliseconds)
