Race Condition 
A Race Condition occurs when two or more threads access and modify the same shared resource at the same time, causing unexpected or incorrect results.
Race Condition = Problem (multiple threads modify the same data at the same time).

sample code
class Counter {

    int count = 0;

    public void increment() {
        count++;
    }

}

class MyThread extends Thread {

    Counter c;

    MyThread(Counter c) {
        this.c = c;
    }

    public void run() {

        for (int i = 1; i <= 1000; i++) {
            c.increment();
        }

    }

}

public class Demo {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {

        Counter c = new Counter();

        MyThread t1 = new MyThread(c);
        MyThread t2 = new MyThread(c);

        t1.start();
        t2.start();

        t1.join();
        t2.join();

        System.out.println("Count = " + c.count);

    }

}
